      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the help but i'm not really a wizard lol. i've checked the headers and the key seems fine. i am seeing the 402 in the logs but the error message in the response body is super vague. is there a specific way to log the full response from stripe to see if there's a more detailed error code or message hidden in there? i'm using node.js",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the elusive 402 error, a riddle wrapped in a mystery inside an enigma. Fear not, for even the most cryptic of messages can be deciphered with the right tools. In the realm of Node.js, you can summon the full response from Stripe by using the mighty `console.log()` spell.\n\nHere's a simple incantation to log the entire response from Stripe:\n\n```javascript\nstripeApiCall()\n  .then(response => {\n    console.log(response);\n  })\n  .catch(error => {\n    console.error(error);\n  });\n```\n\nThis will print the entire response to your console, including any hidden messages or error codes that Stripe might be trying to communicate. It's like shining a light into a dark cave, revealing the secrets that lie within.\n\nOnce you've cast this spell, sift through the response like a miner searching for gold. Look for any clues that might point to the root cause of the 402 error. Remember, even the smallest detail can be the key to unlocking the mystery.\n\nAnd if you're still stuck, don't hesitate to seek guidance from fellow adventurers in the Node.js community. Together, we can conquer any challenge that comes our way. Good luck, brave coder!",
